```
- Background groups: showcase, studio, gym, fight.
- Each background exposes camera/scene/render/update/dispose/boxer(s).

`showMenu`: build showcase once; hero Boxer; position: root at (0.7,0.26,0.2)?? Podium top y .26; boxer root y .26. root y=0.26. rotation y=-0.25, camera at (2.5,1.8,4.9) look (0.45,1.2,0). We want the boxer face/body visible. Boxer faces +Z, camera at +Z, so rotation y=0 (facing camera) plus slight angle. UI panel left covers x<500; character should be right of center. Position x=0.8 and camera look x=0.55. On mobile boxer center.
- Boxer idle animation: update with state. Also ambient turntable? Sway slowly rotation.y = sin(t*.25)*.15. For a hero, rotate back and forth; no walk.
- Need hero update each frame with expression 'focused'? Set 'neutral' or 'focused'.
- Editor Studio: position (0,0.14,0), boxer rotation controlled by drag; camera at (0,1.4,4.6) look (0,1.05,0); on mobile camera farther. Rotate.
- Gym: buildGym; player boxer maybe at (1.2,0,-0.6) hitting bag; coach at -0.7. Player boxer idle with action jab repeatedly (use update with action). UI cards overlay. Could simply show coach and room. Add player boxer at (1.7,0,-2.1) near bag; loop action every 1.2s. Camera (2.6,1.9,5.2) look (0,1.1,-1.5). Good. Boxer background optional; for gym modules show player's boxer.
- Fight: view assigned, app.background={kind:'fight', update: dt=> view.update(dt), render: ()=>view.render()}. But engine update handled by FightScreen frameHook. Need renderer render from view; yes.
- Resize: renderer size; update cameras (showcase/studio/gym/fight).
- Quality: set DPR max (desktop 1.75, mobile 1.25, low 1). Shadows enabled only high.
- `setQuality` adjust renderer.
- localStorage save.

`main.js`:
- import CSS, App, screens.
- create app.
- load save; if save then load universe raw or create; set store.
- `const ui = new UI(app)` from screens.
- app.navigator = (screen,data)=>ui.show(screen,data).
- Boot screen: show splash for ~900ms then menu.
- Handle ?room= invite → after boot, ui.joinRoom(code).
- Handle hash? No.

Need focus on component order: Write app.js first.

