content.text:
Now multiplayer networking module and UI. This is significant. Let's design `src/net/net.js`.

Use PeerJS:
```
import Peer from 'peerjs';
const PREFIX='tgboxing-v1-';
export function normalizeRoom(code){...}
export function roomToPeerId(code){ if code starts 'OPEN' -> 'tgboxing-open-<n>' else 'tgboxing-p-<code>' }
export function randomCode(){ 5 chars no ambiguous }
```
PeerJS peer id restrictions: alphanumeric, -, _ allowed. fine.

`class NetSession extends EventTarget` or simple callbacks via `on`. Implement:
```
export class NetSession {
 constructor({role, code, name, profile, onEvent, onStatus, onData, onOpen, onClose})...
 host({publicSlot}) -> create Peer(id)
 join(code) -> new Peer() with random id? Guest Peer can have auto id; connect to host id. Simpler: new Peer() auto id. 
```
Host must own deterministic id. `new Peer(peerId, {debug:1})`.
Guest `new Peer(undefined, {debug:1})`, then on open `peer.connect(hostPeerId, {reliable:true, serialization:'json'})`.
PeerJS default serialization 'binary' might need; use json.

For public slots:
- host `public:true` chooses slot 0..7, peerId `tgboxing-open-<slot>`.
- Guest quickJoin: try slots sequentially via guest Peer? A single Peer can make multiple connections but to different peers; if slot unavailable, connection error. We can instantiate a temporary Peer per attempt with timeout. Simpler: quick search uses `fetch('https://0.peerjs.com/peerjs/id...')`? No.
- Use each attempt: create a new Peer() guest, connect to slot id with 2.5s timeout; if open -> resolve; else destroy and next. Sequential up to 8 = 20s worst. Could parallel 8 peers, but heavy. Use 4 slots maybe. We'll do 8 with 1.6s timeout parallel? Browser can handle 8 WebSocket signaling connections. But each Peer creates WebSocket to cloud; okay-ish. Use parallel with Promise.any-like manual. On first success, destroy others. That gives quick match. Implement `quickJoin({onStatus})` in net.js.

Reconnection:
- Host: peer on 'disconnected' -> peer.reconnect(); on 'error' type 'unavailable-id' maybe room collision; surface.
- Guest: on connection close, attempt reconnect to host id up to 5 with delay 1s (peer still open) using peer.connect. If peer disconnected, peer.reconnect() then connect.
- Heartbeat: host sends snapshot with timestamp anyway; guest sends ping every 2s; host pong. If no data for 8s -> status reconnecting. We'll manage in UI.

Protocol:
All messages `{t:'type', ...}`.
Guest→host:
- `hello` {name, profile, appearance, record, division, wager, version}
- `ready` {ready}
- `input` {input, seq}
- `punch` {type}
- `chat` {text}
- `rematch` {}
- `forfeit` {}
- `ping` {ts}
Host→guest:
- `welcome` {host info, roomCode, public, wager, maxRounds}
- `peer` {info?} (when host receives hello, sends to UI)
- `start` {config:{rounds, difficulty}, p1:{...}, p2:{...}, arenaId, matchId, startAt?}
- `snapshot` {snapshot}
- `event` {events:[...]}
- `result` {result, matchId}
- `pong` {ts}
- `rematch` {ready}
- `chat`
- `forfeit`
- `error` {message}

Host is p1, guest p2.

In UI, create host/guest players:
- Host info = local player info (save profile or guest fallback).
- Guest info from hello.
- Host sends start with both fighter definitions.
- Host engine config with p1 local, p2 remote; AI off; mode multiplayer; rounds 3.
- Guest engine config with p1 host, p2 local guest; apply snapshots.
- Arena chosen host: use random high-tier? Choose based on division/hype; e.g., 'vegas' or host pick? UI can offer arena select in lobby. Include in host config; guest receives.
- Wager: host declares its wager; guest hello declares. Host accepts min(wager values)? If mismatch, use min. Host includes final wager in welcome. Validate guest wager <= guest coins? Host only gets declared; player self-validates on result application. Use `Math.min(hostWager,guestWager)` and cap 5000.
- Wager fraud protection: matchId included in start/result; receipt includes hash. Each side applies idempotently by matchId in local `multiplayer.history` check.

PeerJS cloud server config: default. Could set config with `secure:true`. default automatic. `debug: 0`.

ICE servers: default PeerJS includes STUN? PeerJS cloud default uses Google STUN maybe. Add config:
```
config: { iceServers: [{urls:'stun:stun.l.google.com:19302'},{urls:'stun:global.stun.twilio.com:3478'}] }
```
No TURN, so some NATs fail; note assumption. Real multiplayer works on typical networks.

Net class callbacks:
```
export class NetSession {
 constructor(opts={}) { this.listeners = new Map(); ...}
 on(type, fn)
 emit(type, data)
 host({code, publicSlot})
 join({code})
 send(msg)
 sendToConn(msg)
 destroy()
 setStatus(status, detail)
}
```
Simplify: use EventTarget? Custom.

Implementation details:
```
_createPeer(id) {
 return new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{
  const peer = id ? new Peer(id, {config}) : new Peer({config});
  peer.on('open', id => resolve(peer));
  peer.on('error', err => { ...; reject(err)});
 });
}
```
But host needs error handling after open too. We'll manage in class methods.

Host flow:
```
async host({code, publicSlot}) {
 this.role='host'; this.code = code; this.peerId = code.startsWith('OPEN-') ? `tgboxing-open-${slot}` : `tgboxing-p-${code}`;
 const peer = new Peer(this.peerId,{config,debug:0});
 this.peer=peer;
 peer.on('open', id=>{ this.connected=true; emit('ready',{id,code,role:'host'});});
 peer.on('connection', conn => this._bindConnection(conn));
 peer.on('error', err => this._handleError(err));
 peer.on('disconnected', ()=>{ setStatus('reconnecting'); setTimeout(()=>{try{peer.reconnect()}catch{}},1200)});
 peer.on('close', ()=>emit('closed'));
}
```
Connection bind:
```
if(this.conn){ guest duplicate -> close new with error }
conn.on('open', ()=>{ this.conn=conn; emit('connected'); this._startHeartbeat();});
conn.on('data', data=>this._onMessage(data));
conn.on('close',()=> {emit('disconnected'); this.conn=null; ...});
conn.on('error', ...);
```
Guest flow:
```
async join({hostPeerId, code}) {
 this.role='guest'; this.code=code; this.hostPeerId=hostPeerId;
 create peer with auto id; on open => conn=peer.connect(hostPeerId,{reliable:true, serialization:'json'}); bind; set timeout 8s for connection open -> error.
}
```
On connection open, guest sends hello automatically? We need info; set `this.localInfo` before join. Send hello on open.

Message routing: emit('message', data) plus specific events by `data.t`:
- emit('data', data)
- emit(data.t, data)
Then UI can subscribe.

`send(msg)` sends via conn if open.
For input rate: UI manages.

Quick join public:
```
export async function quickJoin({timeout=2200, slots=8, onStatus}) {
 const attempts = [];
 for slots: attempts.push(trySlot(slot))
 return Promise.any(attempts)...
}
async function trySlot(slot){
  // create peer guest with random id; connect to host id; wait open
}
```
But NetSession.join expects hostPeerId; public code resolution: code `OPEN-<slot>` -> hostPeerId `tgboxing-open-<slot>`. We can implement quickJoin inside NetSession: `joinPublic({slots})` creates 8 NetSession-like? Simpler implement a function that creates Peer objects and resolves with the winning Peer + conn, then wraps into session:
```
async joinPublic({onStatus}) {
  const attempts = Array.from({length:8}, (_, slot)=> this._tryPublicSlot(slot));
  try { const {peer, conn, slot} = await Promise.any(attempts); ...; this._attachPeer(peer); bind conn; send hello; set code `OPEN-${slot}`; }
}
_tryPublicSlot(slot){
 return new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{
   const peer = new Peer({config,debug:0});
   let done=false;
   const timer=setTimeout(()=>{if(!done){done=true;peer.destroy();reject(new Error('timeout'))}},2600)
   peer.on('open', ()=>{
      const conn=peer.connect(`tgboxing-open-${slot}`, {reliable:true,serialization:'json'});
      conn.on('open',()=>{if(done)return;done=true;clearTimeout(timer);resolve({peer,conn,slot});});
      conn.on('error',()=>fail());
   });
   peer.on('error',()=>fail());
 })
}
```
Host public chooses slot random from 0..7 and binds. If ID unavailable (someone else hosts slot), retry another slot. Implement in `hostPublic`:
```
for attempts slots shuffled: try new Peer(`tgboxing-open-${slot}`); if open resolve; if unavailable-id destroy and next.
```
Peer error 'unavailable-id' fires and also 'open' never. Need remove listeners and retry. Implement `_hostOnSlot`.

Private host code random 6 chars. If ID unavailable retry 3.

Automatic reconnect guest:
- `_reconnectTimer` after conn close. `this.reconnectAttempts`. Attempt `this.peer.connect(this.hostPeerId)`. If peer disconnected, `this.peer.reconnect()`.
- Before retry, if peer open, connect; bind; on open send hello (resume flag) and emit('reconnected').
- Host on connection close: keep room open for guest to reconnect; UI show "aguardando reconexão".
- Host if peer disconnected: peer.reconnect.

Heartbeat:
- setInterval every 2500: guest send ping; host send snapshot anyway. Track lastMessage; if guest stale >9s set status.
- Interval cleanup on destroy.

Serialization: `serialization:'json'` supported.

Net errors mapping to PT messages.

Also `sanitizeInfo` maybe.

Let's write net.js.

